-- l4 batch over an exported rule whose body calls an overloaded `scaled` at a
-- named site that leaves out `rate`, the input only the first `scaled` defaults.
-- The second `scaled` takes a STRING for `base` and the request's `n` is a
-- NUMBER, so the written input settles which rule the site means and the
-- default is taken (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md, the overload decision O3).
-- The same two rules with a NUMBER `base` in both leave the site ambiguous
-- (not-ok/tc/typically-overloaded-site.l4).
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 3
      base IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS rate TIMES base

GIVEN base IS A STRING
      factor IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
scaled MEANS factor

@export default Combine the pieces
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE combine IS scaled WITH base IS n
